Executive Summary
This report documents a network discovery assessment performed within a controlled home lab environment. The objective was to identify active services exposed by a Windows virtual machine using Nmap and to develop a better understanding of network reconnaissance techniques.

Scope
Scanner: Kali Linux Virtual Machine
Target: Windows Virtual Machine
Tool Used: Nmap
Environment: VirtualBox Home Lab

Assessment Objectives

The purpose of this assessment was to:

Identify accessible hosts
Discover open ports
Identify running services
Understand how systems communicate across networks
Practice security documentation

Methodology

Step 1
Identified the target system IP address using:

ipconfig
Step 2
Performed a basic Nmap scan:

nmap <target-ip>
Step 3
Performed service detection:

nmap -sV <target-ip>
Step 4
Reviewed scan results and documented observations.

