Analysis
During the assessment, several network services were identified on the target system.

Questions considered during analysis:

Why are these services available?
Are they required for normal system operation?
Could any services increase the attack surface?
What information can be gathered from service detection?

The scan demonstrated how Nmap can be used to gather information about a system before conducting further analysis.

Lessons Learned
During this exercise I learned:

How Nmap performs network discovery
The relationship between IP addresses and ports
How services communicate over a network
The importance of reconnaissance within cybersecurity
How attackers and defenders can both use network scanning techniques

Reflection
This lab provided practical experience using Nmap to investigate a target system within a controlled environment. Through network discovery and service enumeration, I gained a better understanding of how systems expose services and how security professionals gather information during the early stages of an assessment.
